  "summary": "Paper pressed with raised designs using letterpress techniques without ink.",
  "description": "Embossed letterpress creates three-dimensional designs on paper through pressure alone, without ink, resulting in subtle tactile relief. This technique emerged alongside letterpress printing and became popular for stationery, book covers, and official documents.",
